### Extended Catalog Smell (bonus finding)

#### 10. Assertion Roulette
**Ref:** Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020  
**Test:** `CalculateTotal_ReturnsCorrectAmount` (line 69)

```csharp
// ❌ 3 assertions with no message parameters
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount);
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m, order.TaxAmount);
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal);
```

**Risk:** When one fails, the MSTest output shows *"Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<X>. Actual:<Y>"* — you must read the source to know which property was wrong.

**Fix — add message parameters:**
```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(expectedSubtotal, order.TotalAmount, "Subtotal mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(expectedTax, order.TaxAmount, "Tax mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(expectedTotal, order.GrandTotal, "Grand total mismatch");
```

