## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Effort | Why first |
|----------|-------|------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | `ProcessOrder_CompletesWithoutError` | Low | False-pass risk — verifies nothing |
| 2 | Mystery Guest | `ImportOrders_FromCsv_ParsesCorrectly` | Low | Broken on every CI run (hard-coded Windows path) |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | `ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent` | Medium | Flakiness source + 2 s slowdown per run |
| 4 | Conditional Test Logic | `ProcessOrder_SetsCorrectStatus` | Low | One branch is always untested |
| 5 | Exception Handling | `ProcessOrder_EmptyOrder_ThrowsValidationError` | Low | Quick swap to `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>` |
| 6 | Magic Number + Assertion Roulette | `CalculateTotal_ReturnsCorrectAmount` | Medium | Readability and diagnostic clarity |
| 7 | Sensitive Equality | `GetOrderSummary_ReturnsFormattedString` | Medium | Brittle to formatting changes |
| 8 | Eager Test | `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` | Medium | Hard to diagnose failures |
| 9 | General Fixture | Class-wide (`_logger`) | Low | Remove one unused field |

